# =============================================================================
# Simple Taxi Fleet Simulator - API Test Suite (Kulala.nvim)
# =============================================================================
# Atajos útiles en Neovim con kulala.nvim:
#   <leader>Rr  -> Ejecutar la petición bajo el cursor
#   <leader>Ra  -> Ejecutar todas las peticiones secuencialmente
#   <leader>Rt  -> Alternar vista entre cuerpo (body) y cabeceras
#   <leader>Rc  -> Copiar la petición actual como comando cURL
#   <leader>Rn  -> Saltar a la siguiente petición
#   <leader>Rp  -> Saltar a la petición anterior
# =============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 0. Healthcheck & Ping
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# @name ping
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Gestión de Conductores (PostgreSQL)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Crear Conductor (Carlos Sainz)
# @name createDriver1
POST {{baseUrl}}/drivers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Carlos Sainz",
  "status": "AVAILABLE"
}

### 1.2 Crear Segundo Conductor (Fernando Alonso)
# @name createDriver2
POST {{baseUrl}}/drivers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fernando Alonso",
  "status": "AVAILABLE"
}

### 1.3 Listar Todos los Conductores
# @name getDrivers
GET {{baseUrl}}/drivers
Accept: application/json

### 1.4 Consultar Conductor por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/drivers/{{createDriver1.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Gestión de Vehículos (PostgreSQL)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Crear Vehículo Taxi
# @name createVehicle
POST {{baseUrl}}/vehicles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "plate": "5555-MAD",
  "licenseNumber": "TX-055",
  "status": "AVAILABLE",
  "latitude": 404168,
  "longitude": -37038
}

### 2.2 Listar Vehículos
# @name getVehicles
GET {{baseUrl}}/vehicles
Accept: application/json

### 2.3 Asignar Vehículo al Conductor 1
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/drivers/{{createDriver1.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assignedVehicleId": {{createVehicle.response.body.id}}
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Ciclo de Vida del Turno / Servicio (Redis + Postgres + MongoDB)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 Solicitar Turno en Tiempo Real (Se guarda en Redis como PENDING)
# @name createShift
POST {{baseUrl}}/shifts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientName": "Pedro Ortega",
  "from": "Puerta del Sol, Madrid",
  "to": "Aeropuerto Adolfo Suárez Barajas T4"
}

### 3.2 Consultar Estado Activo del Turno en Redis (Debe ser PENDING)
GET {{baseUrl}}/shifts/{{createShift.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 3.3 Conductor Acepta el Turno (Pasa a ONTHEWAY, flota a BUSY en Postgres)
# @name acceptShift
POST {{baseUrl}}/shifts/{{createShift.response.body.id}}/accept
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "driverId": {{createDriver1.response.body.id}}
}

### 3.4 Verificar en Redis que el Turno ahora está ONTHEWAY
GET {{baseUrl}}/shifts/{{createShift.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 3.5 Verificar en PostgreSQL que el Conductor y Vehículo están BUSY
GET {{baseUrl}}/drivers/{{createDriver1.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 3.6 Completar el Turno (Mueve a MongoDB, libera flota a AVAILABLE y borra de Redis)
# @name completeShift
POST {{baseUrl}}/shifts/{{createShift.response.body.id}}/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fare": 38.50
}

### 3.7 Comprobar que el Turno YA NO EXISTE en Redis (Debe devolver 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/shifts/{{createShift.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json

### 3.8 Comprobar en PostgreSQL que el Conductor vuelve a estar AVAILABLE
GET {{baseUrl}}/drivers/{{createDriver1.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Histórico de Turnos Archivados (MongoDB)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 Listar todos los Turnos Archivados en MongoDB
# @name getShiftHistory
GET {{baseUrl}}/shift-histories
Accept: application/json

### 4.2 Filtrar Histórico por Conductor
GET {{baseUrl}}/shift-histories?filter=%7B%22where%22%3A%7B%22driverName%22%3A%22Carlos%20Sainz%22%7D%7D
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Operadores / Usuarios (In-Memory DB)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5.1 Crear Operador
# @name createUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Admin Central",
  "email": "central@taxifleet.com",
  "password": "supersecretpassword123",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### 5.2 Listar Operadores
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Accept: application/json
